<!--
  UniFi switch (USW) syslog decoders
  Astier Consulting - https://www.astier-consulting.fr

  Observed formats. MACs below are documentation values (RFC 7042 range
  00-00-5E-00-53-xx), not live equipment.

    A. <mac>,<model>: <facility>: <daemon>[pid]: <message>
       00005e005301,USW-Pro-Max-48-7.5.4+17029: mcad: mcad[883]: ui-ubus-utils...
    B. <mac>,<model>: <facility>: <COMPONENT>: <message>          <-- no pid
       00005e005302,USW-Enterprise-24-PoE-7.5.9+17125: switch: LOOP_PROT: Is looped...
    C. <mac>,<model>: <facility>: <message>                       <-- no component
       00005e005303,USW-Flex-2.5G-5-7.4.2.1039: switch: Port:4 link up, Speed: 2500M
    D. <mac>,<model>: <daemon>[pid]: <message>
       00005e005302,USW-Enterprise-24-PoE-7.5.9+17125: udhcpc[951]: sending renew

  A previous revision required `(?:\[\d+\])+`, i.e. a PID, so only A and D
  matched. B and C fell through with the daemon and message fields empty,
  rendering the rule as "UniFi switch []: ". On a sampled deployment that was
  99.9% of unifi-sw traffic, and it silently dropped LOOP_PROT (loop detection),
  DOT1X/DOT1S, FDB rewrites and link state changes.

  The optional second label is restricted to UPPERCASE component names or
  daemon[pid] so that "Port:4 link up" (format C) is NOT split at "Port:".

  NOTE: on hosts that also load the BNC community UniFi decoders
  (bnc_unifi_decoders.xml), those define a `unifi-switch` decoder that loads
  first and claims these lines, firing the generic OSSEC rule 1002 ("Unknown
  problem somewhere in the system"). Exclude the BNC decoders in ossec.conf
  (<decoder_exclude>bnc_unifi_decoders.xml</decoder_exclude>) so this decoder
  can run. (Clean installs without BNC need no change.)
-->
<decoder name="unifi-sw">
  <prematch type="pcre2">^[0-9a-fA-F]{12},USW-\S+:\s</prematch>
</decoder>
<decoder name="unifi-sw-fields">
  <parent>unifi-sw</parent>
  <regex type="pcre2">^[0-9a-fA-F]{12},(\S+?):\s+(\S+?)(?:\[\d+\])?:\s+(?:([A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{2,}|\S+?\[\d+\]):\s+)?(.*)</regex>
  <order>sw_model, sw_facility, sw_component, sw_message</order>
</decoder>
